course: dictionary
lesson: 10248
title: A word from the school fete
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one place, and you learn them by knowing where they are used. «The parents of both streets even ran a summer fete together, and argued only about the tombola.» Fete is a fair, and the tombola is one of the things at that fair.
explain: Read the words around the new word for clues. The sentence says there was a summer fete, so a tombola is probably something you find at a fair. People argued about it, so it must be something people cared about winning. Try your meaning in the sentence: «argued only about a game at the fair» still makes sense.
explain: A tombola is a game where you buy a ticket. If your ticket number matches a number on a prize, you win. The turning drum holds the tickets, and it is part of the game too.
fact: A tombola is a game at a fair. People buy tickets, and they win a prize if their number matches.
fact: The turning drum that tickets are drawn from is also called a tombola.
fact: Tombolas are common at school fetes, church fairs and Christmas fairs in the UK and Ireland.
fact: Prizes are often bottles, sweets and toys, and parents often give them.
fact: The tombola is used to raise money for the school or the church.
exercise: «The parents ran a summer fete, and argued only about the tombola.» What is a tombola? | A type of school bag | A kind of ride at the seaside | *A game at a fair where a ticket number wins a prize | A cake sold at the fair
exercise: In «The parents ran a summer fete together, and argued only about the tombola.» what might the tombola be part of? | A school bus | A bedtime story | *A summer fete | A long car journey
exercise: What is the turning drum in a tombola used for? | To play music for the crowd | *To pick out the tickets | To hold the cakes | To keep the prizes cold
test: Ada buys a ticket at the tombola. What does she hope for? | To get a free dinner | To be sent home early | *To win a prize if her ticket number matches one on a prize | To sell her toys
test: Where would you most likely find a tombola? | *At a school fete or church fair | On a football pitch at night | In the middle of a library's history section | Inside a fridge
exam: If only one ticket out of 100 wins, is your chance of winning a big chance or a small chance? | A certain win | An impossible win | *A small chance | A big chance
